#
# Runtime implementation boundary ledger, enforced by
# scripts/check_runtime_boundary.py and documented in
# docs/runtime-boundary.md.
#
# Every C file under runtime/ must be registered here as exactly one line:
#
#   <category> <ceiling> <path>
#
# `ceiling` is the maximum line count admitted for that file. The check fails
# when a file grows past its ceiling or when an unregistered C file appears, so
# the boundary cannot erode one small commit at a time.
#
# Categories
#
#   host          A genuine platform, libc, or toolchain ABI operation that
#                 Weave cannot yet express directly and safely. Policy-
#                 compliant. A new `host` entry must carry a `why:` comment
#                 stating what Weave cannot express; keep it mechanical, and
#                 delete it when the Weave capability lands.
#
#   port-pending  Pre-existing portable language behavior that the policy says
#                 belongs in Weave, kept only until it is ported. Issue #432
#                 owns the port. Ceilings here are a ratchet: they may be
#                 lowered as code moves to Weave, and a raise is a deliberate,
#                 reviewable line in this file that needs a stated reason. Do
#                 not add new `port-pending` entries — new portable behavior
#                 goes in src/ as Weave.
#
# Lowering a ceiling after porting is encouraged and needs no justification.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# host — platform and toolchain ABI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# why: fork/exec of clang and llc, and host CPU feature flags.
host 320 runtime/llvm_toolchain.c
# why: realpath and platform path validation against the host filesystem.
host 215 runtime/path_safety.c
# why: POSIX write/open/flush and host IEEE bit conversion; weavec1 cannot
# compile f64 compiler sources, so Weave cannot own the bit step yet.
host 461 runtime/portable.c
# why: argv/argc access for produced programs.
host 24 runtime/process_args.inc
# why: private runtime linked into produced programs, not into the compiler.
host 23 runtime/program.c
# why: test-only quantum stub; production behavior is out of scope per
# CONTRIBUTING.md.
host 272 runtime/quantum_runtime.c

